# RG2 = G2 / G3 / G4 (round G-core), guest g: the k2 character is its online character (uploaded before the run, its
# own online story seeded from the card: phase 2, K0-K2). The title calls it; the Game Start gives it the owner's story:
# phase 6 and K0-K10 (none of its own phase 2). It saves in the save room (stagML12's save Digi-Elf, stagIS12): the
# save room writes the engine's records, which hold the owner's story, but its card store writes its own story (run.py
# "own_story": every used box of the online card and of every backup, the stored story's revision unchanged, the local
# card folder empty). Then the lobby gate offers stag0401, whose K9 / K10 entrance opens (905).
campaign until stage=stagml11
talk until control,frames>=60
log in the lobby
idle until frames>=60 fail flag:6=0,flag:2=1,key:9=0,key:10=0
log the owner's story: phase 6, K0-K10
mat matz00 yes until stage=stagml12,control
log in stagml12
errand save:n_digilfm#0 stagml12 until stage=stagis12
log in the save room
campaign until stage=stagml12,control
log back from the save room
idle until frames>=60 fail flag:6=0,key:10=0
log still the owner's story
mat matz00 yes until stage=stagml11,control
log back in the lobby
explore mate00 until onme:mate00
gate mate00 3 until stage=stag0401,control
log in stag0401
idle until frames>=60 fail flag:905=0
log the K9 / K10 entrance is open
idle until frames>=120
